# THE LAST LIGHT · Chapter 3 · The Storm

== ch3_forecast mode=radio
! static
MORAG: All stations, all stations, this is Stornoway Coastguard. Gale warning. Hebrides, Minches: south-westerly severe gale nine, increasing storm ten, imminent. Visibility very poor. Stornoway out.
~ Ten. The windows are already shivering in their frames.

== ch3_corrie mode=radio
! static
CORRIE: North Point, Corrie May. Coming in from the east, and the sea's gone mad. I've lost the shore lights altogether. Over.
CALLUM: Corrie May, North Point. I'll put you in the East Gut. Confirm your position when I call. Over.

== ch3_lowestoft mode=radio
! static
LOWESTOFT: North Point Light, Lowestoft Star, Lowestoft Star. Running before it from the north. Can't hold her head up. Advise, over.
CALLUM: Lowestoft Star, North Point. Stand by. I've another boat on the East Gut. You're next. Over.
LOWESTOFT: Don't be long, North Point.

== ch3_after_two mode=thought
[if saved("Corrie May") and saved("Lowestoft Star")] ~ Both in. Both in. The engine's knocking like a fist on a table.
[if lost("Corrie May") or lost("Lowestoft Star")] ~ The radio fills up with Morag's voice and the lifeboat's, and then with nothing at all.
~ Two o'clock coming. The worst of it still to come.

== ch3_elspeth mode=radio
! static
ELSPETH: North Point Light, this is motor vessel Iona Star, Iona Star. Passage report, over.
CALLUM: Iona Star, North Point. Go ahead, over.
ELSPETH: Glasgow for Stornoway, twelve souls aboard. We expect to pass abeam of your light at oh-five-hundred. Request local conditions, over.
CALLUM: Severe gale nine, storm ten imminent. Seas very high off the Gut. Keep well out to the east until you're past. Over.
ELSPETH: Understood. Keep well east. Who am I speaking to, North Point? Over.
* Callum Mackay, principal keeper. Over. -> name
* North Point Light. That's all you need. Over. -> curt
= name
ELSPETH: Mackay.
! wait 1.2
ELSPETH: My father's boat was lost under your light, Mr Mackay. Eighteen years ago tonight.
ELSPETH: This is Elspeth Ross. First mate. I wanted you to know who was out here.
* I'm sorry, Miss Ross. I was there that night. -> sorry_there
* I know who your father was. -> know
* (Say nothing.) -> silence
= sorry_there
! add rel.elspeth 1
! set told_elspeth_there=1
ELSPETH: ...Were you. Then you'll keep your light burning tonight. Iona Star out.
-> END
= know
ELSPETH: Everyone knows who my father was. That was rather the point of the Inquiry. Iona Star out.
-> END
= silence
! add rel.elspeth -1
ELSPETH: ...Iona Star out.
-> END
= curt
! add rel.elspeth -1
ELSPETH: Thank you, North Point. That is all I need. Iona Star out.

== ch3_notes_a mode=radio
! static
MORAG: North Point, Stornoway. Callum, are you there? Over.
CALLUM: I'm here.
MORAG: I've something I should have said a long time ago. I've got it in front of me. My notebook from that night. Pencil. I kept it in my handbag for eighteen years like a fool.
MORAG: Mayday from Mary Ellen received at oh-one-fifty-two. And what he said was:
MORAG: "No light at North Point. Repeat. No light"

== ch3_dark mode=thought
! static fade
~ Bang. The room goes black.
~ Lamps out. Radio dead. Above my head the clockwork slows and stops.
~ Only the red lamp on the distribution cabinet, glowing like a coal. The main breaker.

== ch3_notes_b mode=radio
! static
MORAG: ...North Point! Callum! Answer me!
CALLUM: Lost the main breaker. I'm back. Light's back. Over.
MORAG: Thank God. Callum, did you hear what I said? Oh-one-fifty-two. No light. Your father's log says the light failed at oh-two-ten. After she struck.
MORAG: Eighteen minutes, Callum. They hanged Alasdair Ross's name on eighteen minutes.
* The log says oh-two-ten. The log is right. -> lie
* Morag, it was eighteen years ago. What does it matter now? -> deflect
* I was there. The light was out before she struck. -> admit
= lie
! set lied_to_morag=1
! add rel.morag -2
MORAG: ...Right.
MORAG: Right. I'll write that in my log, then. "North Point confirms the log." Stornoway out.
-> END
= deflect
! set deflected_morag=1
! add rel.morag -1
MORAG: It matters to the seven men's widows. It matters to his girl. It matters to me, Callum. Stornoway out.
-> END
= admit
! set admitted_to_morag=1
! add rel.morag 2
MORAG: ...Oh, Callum.
MORAG: Not on the air. Not now. When this blows through, you and I are going to sit at my kitchen table. Stornoway listening.

== ch3_rory_dark mode=radio
! static
RORY: North Point, Kittiwake. Callum, you'll think I'm daft. Over.
CALLUM: Go ahead, Rory.
RORY: I'm tied up in the Sound, and I've been watching. There's a boat came out from the lee of Pabbay. Old wooden boat, a wee motor-fisher. No lights. Not a single light, Callum.
RORY: She's heading your way. Not for the Sound. For your landing, under the light. Over.
~ On the radar a small hard echo is moving in from the north, steady as a clock.
